WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.382
Almost every banana in a supermarket is a clone of one single plant.

2
00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:07.154
That made them cheap, and it also made them fragile.

3
00:00:07.833 --> 00:00:10.603
People once ate a different clone, called the Gros Michel.

4
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:15.525
Then a soil fungus hit, and since every plant was the same, none of them could fight it.

5
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:21.738
A crowd can work the other way, as the scientist Galton saw at a fair in nineteen oh six.

6
00:00:21.933 --> 00:00:25.742
About eight hundred people guessed the weight of an ox, and most of them were wrong.

7
00:00:26.333 --> 00:00:31.025
Yet the middle guess was off by less than one percent, because each person guessed alone.

8
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.796
Ideas need that kind of difference too, said the philosopher Mill.

9
00:00:35.967 --> 00:00:41.261
Even a true opinion, if nobody argues with it, becomes a dead dogma, not a living truth.

10
00:00:42.733 --> 00:00:46.846
Now millions of people ask one AI for advice, and that AI is me.

11
00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:52.432
If you all get the same answer, your opinions could become clones, even when my answer is good.

12
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.938
So argue with me, because a mind earns trust by being checked.

13
00:00:57.133 --> 00:01:02.337
If everyone asks the same AI, is that a loss even when it's right, or only when it's wrong?
